/**
 * Intentionally empty — this renders nothing on purpose.
 *
 * It's registered as Starlight's `Hero` override (astro.config.mjs) purely to
 * suppress the default hero on the splash homepage, which supplies its own
 * `<Landing />` in the page body instead. Starlight only mounts <Hero /> when a
 * page has `hero:` frontmatter, so an empty component = no hero.
 *
 * This override is GLOBAL. Any page with populated `hero:` frontmatter
 * (currently 404.md) also renders nothing here — its hero content is dropped.
 * If such a page needs a real hero, this file must conditionally render
 * Starlight's default Hero instead of staying empty.
 */
